nd the sheer freedom of  movement with these tools equals a lot  less camping which is what most people  usually hate and leads to a lot more  fast-paced range combat which is what  people enjoy also the spawn beacon being  handed to the engineer means no more  whack-a-mole number three sniper rifles  damage vehicles in hardline ever since  the recon player lost the mortar strike  post Bad Company 2  they've been left staring at distant  tanks and ellaby's with really no good  options  hardline has changed the equation by  allowing both action rifles to deal  significant damage to most vehicles  including being superb at shooting down  helicopters translation it's a fair  fight  number 4 LEvolution you can just kill  that word already has more of an impact  on the professional class if you're a  class other than professional the dust  storm really doesn't affect you that  much  a sniper duel on that map would have  distinct phases the first part would be  more methodical long-range combat the  latter phase ending with close-range  secondary weapons as visibility drops  overall evolution with the professional  is just more meaningful and number 5 a  change of pace is kind of nice  I'm not saying that I want to play a  sniper focused mode all night long but I  am saying I would appreciate heist  Hotwire and other modes much more if I  could take a patient group every once in  a while  weird I'm getting a tower mixed mode  playlists make it hot then slow it down  for around  so what would your ideal sniping  centrist mode look like in battlefield  did you catch that awesome co-op sniping  mission from battlefield 3 drop them  like liquid do you hate snipers do you  really just hate yourself or do you just  hate snipers that don't btfo leave your  thoughts in the comments below and we  will see you in about a month when  hardline releases  you
 

